From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:23:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] flash: the review's findings on the frame path (T-576)

An answer to a frame sent before Destroy no longer posts a draw on a dead instance. JihadShow takes no wrap of the
shared surface when a copy fails: it answers at once and the child draws there again, so the frame is dropped. The
lane's source is this frame's copy or nothing. The floor between draws is per instance, the pump's count of posted
draws counts. The proof takes an effect as one item with its own bounds (a transformed overlay's children are in
their own coordinates) and returns where the plugin is now; jihad_offscreen_popups_open: a popup is a display root of
its own. The plugin stays silent only as the one instance on its page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
